  "verbalization": "Azelastine is associated with Vasomotor Rhinitis through a chain of indications that link it to Allergic Rhinitis, which in turn is indicated to several agents that ultimately target Vasomotor Rhinitis. This suggests a potential pathway where Azelastine may exert its effects through mechanisms that are indirectly linked to vasomotor symptoms, possibly by modulating inflammatory or neurogenic responses. The evidence from the three paths is consistent, with Azelastine acting as a bridge to Allergic Rhinitis, which then connects to Vasomotor Rhinitis via different agents. The shared indication of Allergic Rhinitis across all three paths supports a broader role in the pathophysiology of Vasomotor Rhinitis, though the specific mechanisms of action remain unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Allergic Rhinitis as a common intermediate in the relationship between Azelastine and Vasomotor Rhinitis.",
